1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:04,629
Welcome to Melody and
Barnaby's Music Nuggets!

2
00:00:05,629 --> 00:00:10,620
Today we are going to
learn all about octaves.

3
00:00:12,920 --> 00:00:16,564
Look at this group of two black keys.

4
00:00:17,264 --> 00:00:20,768
The white key just below… is C.

5
00:00:24,068 --> 00:00:29,291
Here is another group of
two. And here is another C.

6
00:00:32,991 --> 00:00:34,191
Listen.

7
00:00:37,026 --> 00:00:40,020
The same note… but higher.

8
00:00:43,120 --> 00:00:48,250
From one C to the next
C… is called an octave.

9
00:00:48,950 --> 00:00:50,829
An octave.

10
00:00:54,529 --> 00:01:01,516
It works for F too. From one F
to the next F… is also an octave.

11
00:01:05,616 --> 00:01:11,535
Every C on the piano… is the
same note… higher or lower.

12
00:01:15,935 --> 00:01:18,975
Your turn! Where is another C?

13
00:01:24,075 --> 00:01:25,275
C

14
00:01:25,725 --> 00:01:26,925
C

15
00:01:29,276 --> 00:01:31,108
Where is another F?

16
00:01:35,808 --> 00:01:37,008
F

17
00:01:37,405 --> 00:01:38,726
You've got it!

18
00:01:40,426 --> 00:01:41,887
Now it's your turn!

19
00:01:41,987 --> 00:01:46,235
Play Octave Hunt, and
find every C and F!

20
00:01:46,335 --> 00:01:48,724
See you for the next Nugget!

